A||||1||Spiff||Radiator fan won't turn on||||9||
Z||000000||Spiff||11-03-2001||07:42 PM||||As the title states, my radiator fan won't turn on. <BR>Here is what happened. I went on a drive for about 20 minutes. Then went to wal-mart for about 30 minutes finished shopping and went to McDonalds for some munchies. I was waiting in the drive thru for about 15 minutes when I noticed the temp gauge was jumping around and then the temp light comes on.<P>I turned the AC on and nothing, so I shut the car off (still in line at McDonalds). Pop the Front hood and see steam coming out and smell Anti-freeze. I start the car after 2 minutes and get my food and head on down the road. The temp lowers to normal and engine sounds fine as far as I can tell.<P>I need to know how to fix this. I was supposed to go to the MAFOA fall meeting tomorrow but I'm afraid I will hurt the car if I drive it too far.<P>Does anybody have any suggestions on how to fix this. New temp sensor,thermostat? I need help please. This is for an 88 V6 Formula if that helps.||||reg||9
Z||000001||sqoach||11-03-2001||07:49 PM||||Sounds like you need a new fan motor, or a new relay. Those are the most common. You could also possibly have a loose wire, but not likely. You <I>should</I> be ok driving on the highway, cuz the fan doesn't do much for you when driving at high speeds.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
